@startuml
title Backend module structure (NestJS, ADR-0007 / ADR-0012)
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "AppModule" {
  [HealthController] as Health

  package "CommonModule (@Global)" {
    [PrismaService] as Prisma
    [DomainEvents\n(node EventEmitter wrapper)] as Events
    [ApiError] as ApiError
  }

  package "MissionModule" {
    [MissionController] as MC
    [MissionService] as MS
    [PrismaMissionRepository] as MR
    [MissionDispatchSweeper\n(every 10 s)] as Sweeper
  }

  package "MissionResultModule" {
    [MissionResultController] as MRC
    [MissionResultService] as MRS
    [PrismaMissionResultRepository] as MRR
  }

  package "SignalQualityModule" {
    [SignalQualityController] as SQC
    [SignalQualityService\n(snapshot + tile cache + IDW)] as SQS
    [signalQualityConfig] as SQConf
  }
}

database "PostgreSQL" as DB

MC --> MS
MS --> MR
Sweeper --> MR
MR --> Prisma

MRC --> MRS
MRS --> MRR
MRR --> Prisma
MRS ..> Events : emit ResultRevisionFinalized

SQC --> SQS
SQS --> MRR : allApprovedMeasurements()\n(only module import edge)
SQS ..> Events : on ResultRevisionFinalized -> invalidate()
SQS --> SQConf

Prisma --> DB
MR ..> ApiError
MRR ..> ApiError

note bottom of MissionModule
  No dependency on MissionResult or SignalQuality.
  MissionResultRepository reads Mission rows through
  Prisma directly (upload requires state COMPLETED).
end note

note right of Events
  Global exception filter (main.ts) maps ApiError to
  { error } with its status; validation is a global
  ValidationPipe (whitelist, transform); body limit 20 MB;
  CORS origin "*".
end note
@enduml
